From: Quality Playbook v1.5.8 <quality-playbook>
Subject: [PATCH] BUG-001: re-add VIRTIO_F_NOTIF_CONFIG_DATA in vp_transport_features

vring_transport_features() clears every transport bit it does not enumerate
(default: __virtio_clear_bit), including VIRTIO_F_NOTIF_CONFIG_DATA(39). The
PCI-modern compensator vp_transport_features() re-adds SR_IOV/RING_RESET/ADMIN_VQ
but not bit 39 -- even though vp_check_common_size() validates the common-cfg
queue_notify_data field for it and vp_notify_with_data() can consume it. As a
result the device-offered feature is always cleared and the validated path is dead.

Re-add the bit in the compensator, mirroring the other three.

--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern.c
@@ -376,6 +376,9 @@ static void vp_transport_features(struct virtio_device *vdev, u64 features)
 	if (features & BIT_ULL(VIRTIO_F_RING_RESET))
 		__virtio_set_bit(vdev, VIRTIO_F_RING_RESET);

+	if (features & BIT_ULL(VIRTIO_F_NOTIF_CONFIG_DATA))
+		__virtio_set_bit(vdev, VIRTIO_F_NOTIF_CONFIG_DATA);
+
 	if (features & BIT_ULL(VIRTIO_F_ADMIN_VQ))
 		__virtio_set_bit(vdev, VIRTIO_F_ADMIN_VQ);
 }
